,"distance":0.685,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Kevin O'Connell"}],"defense":[{"season":2023,"team":"GB","distance":0.2472,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2024,"team":"MIA","distance":0.2942,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2025,"team":"IND","distance":0.2979,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Lou Anarumo"},{"season":2022,"team":"DAL","distance":0.3777,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Dan Quinn"},{"season":2024,"team":"CIN","distance":0.3786,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Lou Anarumo"}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Jaguars are 4-2 through week 7 of the 2026 season and have outscored opponents 154 to 104. The offense has been carrying the team, ranking 3rd in EPA per play while the defense sits 13th in EPA allowed. What sets them apart is the 3rd lowest RPO rate in the league.","offense":"The Jaguars have one of the most efficient offenses in the league so far, ranking in the top eight in four of the five main efficiency measures. Their run and pass mix has stayed close to what game situations call for. Schematically, they stand out for the 3rd lowest RPO rate in the league. Trevor Lawrence has run the passing game and leaned heavily on Parker Washington, who has drawn 27% of the targets.","defense":"The Jaguars defense has been a little above average by EPA allowed per play so far. It has been much better against the run than the pass, ranking 3rd and 13th. Travon Walker has led the way with 2 sacks. Their scheme has been fairly conventional, and the closest thing to a signature is an eight man box rate that ranks 6th highest in the league.","special":"The Jaguars have been one of the most conservative teams on fourth down, going for it on only 14% of their short-yardage chances. Their kickers have made 83% of field goals, which is about average. Their salary cap was spread across positions in a fairly typical way.","players":"Trevor Lawrence has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 1,480 yards. Parker Washington has been the clear top target with 27% of the looks and 416 receiving yards. Bhayshul Tuten has handled most of the work in the backfield with 64% of the carries. On defense, Travon Walker leads the team with 2 sacks and Foyesade Oluokun has picked off 2 passes.","coaching":"Liam Coen is calling the offense as head coach and Anthony Campanile is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2023 Browns under Kevin Stefanski and the 2024 Buccaneers under Liam Coen. Their defense looks most like the 2023 Packers and the 2024 Dolphins.","trends":"The offense went from 14th in EPA per play in 2025 to 3rd so far this season, a big step forward. The defense moved from 3rd in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 13th so far this season, a big step back. The biggest change in approach was pass rate over expected, which went from 1.64 to -3.2.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}